## Configuration — Connecting a Model

Continue stores its settings in a file called `config.json` (or `config.yaml` in newer versions) which lives at `C:\Users\YourName\.continue\`. You can open it from inside VS Code using the Continue settings panel.

Here's a minimal configuration connecting Continue to Claude via the Anthropic API:

```json
{
  "models": [
    {
      "title": "Claude Sonnet",
      "provider": "anthropic",
      "model": "claude-sonnet-4-5",
      "apiKey": "YOUR_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
    }
  ],
  "tabAutocompleteModel": {
    "title": "Claude Haiku (autocomplete)",
    "provider": "anthropic",
    "model": "claude-haiku-4-5",
    "apiKey": "YOUR_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
  }
}
```

You can also add Ollama models (covered in Part 12) for fully local, private code assistance with no API key needed:

```json
{
  "models": [
    {
      "title": "Llama 3 (local)",
      "provider": "ollama",
      "model": "llama3"
    }
  ]
}
```
